        <p style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
            Sophisticated malware avoids detection by unlinking its <code>EPROCESS</code> block from the OS scheduler's doubly linked list (<code>ActiveProcessLinks</code>). While invisible to user-mode monitors like Task Manager and Volatility's <code>pslist</code>, its execution structures remain detectable in physical memory pool tags (<code>psscan</code>) and thread scheduler tables.
        </p>

        <h2 class="sub-title">Cross-View Comparison Matrix (DKOM Carving)</h2>
